6ex\" height=\"2.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.338ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 812 936.9\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-12-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-12-Title\">{\\color{red}\\mathcal{C}}.</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E12-MJCAL-43\" d=\"M201 -25Q167 -25 136 -14T75 23T29 94T12 202Q12 290 50 394T161 574Q227 642 303 673T433 704Q435 705 457 705Q533 701 533 640Q533 606 507 548T464 474Q431 444 396 444Q381 444 381 453Q381 459 388 473T407 513T428 563Q433 580 433 594Q433 636 381 636Q314 636 260 594T175 489T128 363T112 247Q112 157 153 101T273 44Q347 44 398 121Q413 144 437 157T481 171Q496 171 496 160Q496 150 476 123Q426 56 350 16T201 -25Z\"></path>\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E12-MJMAIN-2E\" d=\"M78 60Q78 84 95 102T138 120Q162 120 180 104T199 61Q199 36 182 18T139 0T96 17T78 60Z\"></path>\n</defs>\n<g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<g fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\">\n<g fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\">\n<g fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\">\n<g fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\">\n<g fill=\"red\" stroke=\"red\">\n <use xlink:href=\"#E12-MJCAL-43\"></use>\n</g>\n</g>\n</g>\n</g>\n</g>\n <use xlink:href=\"#E12-MJMAIN-2E\" x=\"533\" y=\"0\"></use>\n</g>\n</svg></span></p>\n<p>The diagram below is a commutative diagram that shows how a change of basis works at each step.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-a695280bac50838abdb4d5880dc915a1\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/a695280bac50838abdb4d5880dc915a1\"></div>\n\n<p>Here, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. So algebraically, we can write this as</p>\n<p><span class=\"mjpage mjpage__block\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"25.428ex\" height=\"3.176ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.838ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -1006.6 10948.3 1367.4\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/200